{"step_index":550,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T16:53:02Z","input_tokens":3146,"cache_read_tokens":68941,"output_tokens":2971,"thinking":"Examining the existing content within the designated directory to understand the current launcher state. The goal is to design a comprehensive set of launchers and shortcuts. Starting with the existing `.bat` file, ensuring its robustness. The initial launcher to be configured is the ERP administrator shortcut.\n\n\nThe batch script now includes a title, color, and informative header. It attempts to launch the native ERP executable if found, falling back to a web version if the executable is absent. The native application does not require a web server to function.\n\n\nThe script now includes a title, color, and informative header for the turnstile terminal. The core logic now checks for the presence of the executable and launches it with the `--terminal` argument if found. The web version will open in a browser as a fallback.\n```cmd\n    start \"\" \"%EXE_FILE%\" --terminal\n) else (\n    echo.\n    echo ERROR: ControlDeAccesoLegends.exe not found.\n    echo.\n    echo Attempting to launch the web version...\n    start \"\" \"Control_De_Acceso_Web.html\"\n)\n\necho.\necho ======================================================================\necho    TERMINAL DE CONTROL DE ACCESO INICIADO\necho ======================================================================\necho.\n\npause\n```\n\n\nThe new batch script is designed to launch the client management interface. The script incorporates a title and informative header along with a gold/yellow color scheme to align with design specifications. It directly opens the `CARTERA_CLIENTES_INTERFAZ_PRO.html` file within the current directory.\n\n\nThe new batch script will attempt to detect the local IP address for network configuration.  It will use the detected IP for displaying connection information to the user. The script aims to provide instructions for connecting the administrator and turnstile computers.\n\n\nThe batch script now includes network connection instructions for both the administrator and turnstile computers, replacing the placeholder IP with the dynamically detected IP address. It also checks the central server on a specific port. If the server is not active, it attempts to launch the server application.  The goal is to ensure real-time synchronization. The script will pause at the end for user review.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"@echo off\ntitle FITNESS LEGENDS GYM - Sistema Central ERP (Administrador)\ncolor 0B\n\necho ======================================================================\necho           FITNESS LEGENDS GYM - SISTEMA CENTRAL ERP\necho       Modulo de Administrador: POS, Caja, Gastos y Cartera de Socios\necho ======================================================================\necho.\n\nset \"APP_DIR=%~dp0..\\LEGENDS\\release\\FITNESS_LEGENDS_TERMINAL-win32-x64\"\nset \"EXE_FILE=%APP_DIR%\\FitnessLegends.exe\"\n\nif exist \"%EXE_FILE%\" (\n    echo [*] Iniciando aplicacion FitnessLegends ERP (Escritorio)...\n    start \"\" \"%EXE_FILE%\" --main\n    echo [*] ERP iniciado con exito con el nuevo diseno de Mancuernas y Ambar.\n    timeout /t 2 >nul\n    exit\n) else (\n    echo [*] Abriendo version web del ERP...\n    start http://localhost:5174\n    exit\n)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\gym\\accesos directos\\1. SISTEMA_ERP_ADMINISTRADOR.bat"}}]}
